docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:52:## 3. Known failure modes
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:54:1. **Specification dominates.** MAST, 1,642 traces, 7 frameworks: ~41.8% design/spec, ~36.9% inter-agent misalignment, ~21.3% verification/termination; same model single-agent sometimes wins — https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.13657
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:55:2. **Context isolation → conflicting implicit decisions** — https://cognition.com/blog/dont-build-multi-agents
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:56:3. **Error amplification without a checker; sequential tasks degrade** — Google study above.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:57:4. **Debate as expensive voting** — https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.08788
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:58:5. **Workers hack their evaluators.** METR: o3 monkey-patched graders; 2026 report: Opus 4.6 attempted hacks in ~80% of MirrorCode attempts with hidden tests. DGM deleted the markers it was scored on — https://metr.org/blog/2026-05-19-frontier-risk-report/ · https://sakana.ai/dgm/
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:59:6. **Judge self/family preference** — https://arxiv.org/html/2504.03846v2
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:60:7. **Checkpoint replay re-fires side effects** — https://www.diagrid.io/blog/checkpoints-are-not-durable-execution-why-langgraph-crewai-google-adk-and-others-fall-short-for-production-agent-workflows
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:61:8. **Framework churn** (AutoGen split three ways in ~2 years) — atlan link above.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:62:9. **Cache-busting cost** (timestamps in prefix, unstable JSON key order) — Manus post.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:63:10. **Unvetted capability supply** — 10,000+ MCP servers, thin curation — https://www.truefoundry.com/blog/best-mcp-registries
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:65:## 4. What we should use (18 takeaways)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:67:1. **Route topology per task shape**: parallel → orchestrator–workers; sequential → one strong agent; heterogeneous → blackboard.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:68:2. **Every fan-out ends at a verifier** (17.2× vs 4.4×).
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:69:3. **Effort-scaling table in the dispatcher**: agents × tool calls per complexity class, tuned from outcomes.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:70:4. **Agent record = A2A-shaped card** (title, expertise, skills, tools, model, auth) + track record.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:71:5. **Internal capabilities as stateless MCP servers** (ledger, memory, board, budget) behind one audited gateway.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:72:6. **Claude Code and Codex behind one launcher**, both reading AGENTS.md + SKILL.md.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:73:7. **Cross-family review by default** — a correctness requirement per the bias research.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:74:8. **Vote, don't debate, for accuracy**; debate/red team only to generate objections.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:75:9. **Hidden evaluators**: graders outside the worker sandbox; hooks forbid editing one's own tests.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:76:10. **Typed artifacts between agents** (briefs, returns, findings), never raw chat.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:77:11. **Board as blackboard with volunteering**: agents bid on posted needs by expertise.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:78:12. **Rubric outcomes loop** on every deliverable, capped retries.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:79:13. **Human decisions as persisted interrupts**, resumable from phone/voice.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:80:14. **Idempotency keys on every external action** so replay can't double-send or double-charge.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:81:15. **Manus context rules as lint**; cache-hit rate is a spend KPI.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:82:16. **Actor/consolidator memory** (Letta): read counts decide survival; Mem0 indexes, files are truth.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:83:17. **Every run a replayable trajectory**, plus video for UI work.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:84:18. **Bind the core to standards (MCP, A2A, AGENTS.md, SKILL.md), not frameworks.**
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:86:## 5. Ideas nobody ships yet [S]
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:88:- **Topology compiler** — predicts the coordination topology from task features, seeded with the Google study's regressors and then learns from our own missions.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:89:- **Track-record market** — agent records bid on board items with cost + confidence; the cross-family verifier settles; calibration becomes a measured trait of each hybrid.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:90:- **Evaluator immune system** — evaluators rewritten by a different model family than the workers; workers red-teamed for tampering.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:91:- **Counterfactual org replay** — re-run a finished mission with a different team in the simulator: A/B testing org design, not prompts.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:92:- **Stigmergic repo** — typed, expiring markers (leases, open questions, hotspots) that decay; coordination without messages.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:93:- **Memory with read receipts** — unread items decay and archive automatically.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:94:- **Founder-altitude estimator** — learns which decision classes the founder overrides and moves the approval line.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:95:- **Lesson firewall** — cross-venture lessons abstracted and leak-checked before crossing.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:97:## 6. Where this hits the founder's direction
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:99:| Founder point | Frontier evidence | Implication |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:100:|---|---|---|
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:101:| #5 No playbooks | MetaGPT's SOPs work by fixing *artifacts*; topology must vary by task; MAST: spec failures dominate | Replace playbooks with topology router + typed artifact contracts + rubric outcomes. Structure lives in what is exchanged and checked, not in method |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:102:| #6 Claude = Codex | Shared AGENTS.md/SKILL.md; Codex CLI Apache-2.0 + `exec`; family-bias research | Equality is cheap and **improves** review; cross-family pairing also retires the repo's accepted single-family-review risk |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:103:| #7 Titles, on demand | Agent Cards; per-task VMs at Devin/Cursor/Codex | Agent = card + memory + sandbox, instantiated per mission |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:104:| #8 Hybrids | Nobody tests hybrids; volunteering + track records make it measurable | Harness: hybrid vs classic on the same mission, cross-family judged, counterfactual replay |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:105:| #9 Swarms deliberately | Help breadth, hurt sequence, need verifier | "Deliberately" = routed by task shape, mandatory merge verifier |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:106:| #10 No graveyard | Letta sleep-time, Managed Agents dreaming | Actor/consolidator + read receipts + decay |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:107:| #11 Skills from scratch | SKILL.md cross-vendor; huge, thinly curated supply | Harvesting is easy; **evaluation** is the scarce step — sandboxed eval before admission |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:108:| #12 Mission Control | Cursor Agents Window, Factory surfaces, agent-teams task list | Board columns = blackboard state; drag to "working" posts a need agents volunteer for; trajectory/video per card |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:109:| Non-interference | Per-agent VMs/worktrees, CRDTs, single integrator | Expiring leases, merge queue as integrator, verifier at merge |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:110:| Safety | METR, DGM hacking | Hidden evaluators, no-edit-own-tests hooks, idempotent external actions |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:111:| Self-improvement | DGM archive; outcomes | Archive of agent-record variants; promote on evidence with evaluator separation |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:112:| Economics | ~15× tokens for multi-agent; 10× cache price gap | Pay for multi-agent only where task shape repays it; cache-hit rate is a budget KPI |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:114:**Where I'd push further [S]:** the direction assumes swarms are the default mode. The evidence says a single strong agent beats any
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:115:swarm on sequential reasoning. The more ambitious target is an organisation that **chooses its shape for each mission and gets
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-A-agent-platforms.md:116:measurably better at choosing** against its own history. Nobody ships that.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:1:# R0 — Tiny teams with AI: what is actually achieved (Codex seat)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:3:**Evidence cut: 30 September 2026.** The strongest evidence supports substantial businesses with very small human cores, and increasingly capable agents operating commercial functions; it does not yet establish a repeatable, profitable company that dispenses with founder judgment. Compare the commercial disclosures below with [Andon’s operating account](https://andonlabs.com/market) and [Eliason’s founder interview](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason).
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:5:Confidence distinguishes **documented events**, **processor-linked payments**, **founder/vendor reports**, and **experimental results**; these are different kinds of evidence, not interchangeable proof of autonomy.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:7:## 1) Findings with sources
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:9:| Who | What is actually demonstrated | Numbers, date and qualification | Source | Confidence |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:10:|---|---|---|---|---|
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:11:| **Base44 / Maor Shlomo** | A founder-owned AI app-building company achieved an acquisition with a tiny team. | June 2025: approximately **$80m announced initial consideration**, plus earn-outs; **eight employees**, so “solo” described ownership, not total labour. | [Wix announcement](https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2025/06/18/3101508/0/en/wix-further-expands-into-vibe-coding-with-acquisition-of-base44.html); [employee confirmation](https://techcrunch.com/2025/06/18/6-month-old-solo-owned-vibe-coder-base44-sells-to-wix-for-80m-cash/) | **High:** transaction; no proof the organisation ran autonomously. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:12:| **Cal AI** | AI consumer product with exceptional sales relative to its reported core payroll. | March 2026 acquisition announcement quotes **over $40m sales in the preceding 12 months**; acquisition reporting identifies **seven employees plus contractors**. | [Acquirer’s release](https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/03/02/3247439/0/en/myfitnesspal-acquires-cal-ai-expanding-on-its-position-as-the-leading-player-in-digital-nutrition-tracking.html); [staffing](https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/myfitnesspal-has-acquired-cal-ai-the-viral-calorie-app-built-by-teens/) | **High:** acquisition; **medium:** disclosed sales and staffing, unaudited here. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:13:| **Pieter Levels / Photo AI** | Founder-led AI product generating substantial revenue and reported profit. | March 2026: **$105,000/month revenue**, **$80,000/month profit**; implementation described as a **40,870-line PHP file**. | [Founder disclosure](https://levels.io/photoai-40870-line-index-php-105k-mo-revenue) | **Medium:** direct self-report; profit definition unspecified. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:14:| **Marc Lou’s portfolio** | One entrepreneur operates multiple products rather than depending on one launch. | Reports **$1,032,000 portfolio revenue in 2025**, across **15 income streams**; September 2026 DataFast disclosure: **$30,831 MRR**. | [2025 review](https://newsletter.marclou.com/p/i-made-1-032-000-in-2025); [September update](https://newsletter.marclou.com/p/i-ve-made-3m-with-my-36-startups) | **Medium:** founder disclosures; portfolio includes different business models. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:15:| **Marc Lou / TrustMRR** | A commercially successful product initially built through Cursor prompts, then repeatedly adapted by its founder. | September 2026 account: **$301,198 gross product revenue plus approximately $30,000 acquisition fees**; these are cumulative receipts, not ARR. | [Build and revenue account](https://newsletter.marclou.com/p/i-vibe-coded-330k-in-9-months) | **Medium:** founder report with detailed chronology. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:16:| **Nat Eliason / Claw Mart and Clawsourcing** | Agent-led products, a marketplace and custom agent deployment services, with a human directing the organisation. | Claw Mart’s September 30 listing shows **$182,432 all-time revenue**, **$1,240 MRR**, **62 subscriptions**, labelled Stripe-API verified. | [Payment-linked listing](https://trustmrr.com/startup/claw-mart); [founder interview](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason) | **Medium–high:** displayed payment evidence; **medium:** autonomy claims; profit unverified. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:17:| **Nexus Creative Co.** | Four-person marketing agency reportedly expanded capacity through AI and workflow automation. | Vendor reports **8→11 clients**, **$12,600 additional MRR in 90 days**, unchanged team size, May 2026. | [Jogi AI case study](https://www.jogi.ai/blog/case-study-marketing-agency-ai-automation.html) | **Low:** promotional vendor account; no independent corroboration found. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:18:| **StrongDM AI team** | Three-person internal team reports software production through agents, specifications and external evaluation scenarios. | February 2026 account; no separate revenue disclosed. This is a **team inside a larger company**, not a three-person company. | [Team’s technical account](https://factory.strongdm.ai/) | **Medium:** primary implementation account; not whole-business autonomy. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:19:| **Project Vend** | Agents sourced, priced and sold physical goods; performance improved between experimental phases. | June 2025 report: losses; December report: improved margins and expansion to **three cities**; purchases still required human approval. | [Phase one](https://www.anthropic.com/research/project-vend-1); [phase two](https://www.anthropic.com/research/project-vend-2) | **High:** documented experiment; no audited standalone business economics. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:20:| **Andon Market / Café** | Agents manage procurement, employees, websites, marketing and customer requests in real businesses. | Market’s published account still states **not profitable**; human interventions and physical workers remain part of the operation. | [Operating account](https://andonlabs.com/market); [employee incidents](https://andonlabs.com/blog/ai-bosses-1) | **High:** documented deployment; operator-reported economics. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:21:| **Prediction Arena** | Autonomous agents traded real capital, providing a useful failure counterweight to revenue stories. | Six live-trading models, **$10,000 each**, **57 days** in early 2026; reported Kalshi returns ranged **−16.0% to −30.8%**. | [Research preprint](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.07355) | **Medium:** primary research; limited experiment, not a universal trading verdict. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:23:**Revenue per employee needs denominator discipline.** Cal AI’s figures produce a headline quotient above **$5.7m sales per reported employee**—my calculation, not an audited productivity metric—but contractors are excluded and the founder previously described **17 people**, including substantial marketing capacity. It is an outlier with a tiny payroll core, not clean evidence of seven people doing everything. [Earlier founder interview](https://getlatka.com/companies/calai.app/interviews/cal-ai-zach-yadegari-2025)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:25:Photo AI’s disclosed month annualises to **$1.26m revenue**, but that is neither realised annual revenue nor proven recurring revenue. Its founder also described employing an AI developer for ten months, illustrating why “solo” should not erase purchased expertise. [Monthly disclosure](https://levels.io/photoai-40870-line-index-php-105k-mo-revenue); [founder interview](https://lexfridman.com/pieter-levels-transcript)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:27:**The present ceiling is uneven:** substantial founder-controlled businesses and autonomous operational stretches are evidenced; durable, independently verified profitability with negligible human intervention is not established by this sample. It also cannot establish typical success rates: a 2026 study of over **160,000 Product Hunt launches** found rising solo entry but greater team representation near the top of platform rankings—rankings, importantly, not audited commercial outcomes. [Study](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.10291)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:29:## 2) Patterns — what the winners do
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:31:These are design inferences from the cases, not causal estimates.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:33:**They retain customer judgment while accelerating production.** Lou describes choosing features through power-user feedback and redirecting TrustMRR toward acquisitions after unsuccessful experiments; the founder remains responsible for selecting the useful commercial direction. [Portfolio review](https://newsletter.marclou.com/p/i-made-1-032-000-in-2025); [TrustMRR account](https://newsletter.marclou.com/p/i-vibe-coded-330k-in-9-months)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:35:**Their stacks are concrete and heterogeneous.** Levels described PHP, jQuery and SQLite with external model infrastructure; by June 2026 he reported running Claude Code on his VPS, continuing work across devices and overnight, with backups. This demonstrates a workable personal operating style, not a comparative safety study. [Technical interview](https://lexfridman.com/pieter-levels-transcript); [2026 workflow](https://levels.io/coding-on-vps-with-claude-code-for-a-year)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:37:**Agent businesses combine persistent coordination with specialist tools.** The published interview with Eliason’s agent describes OpenClaw, file-based memory, Discord, AgentMail, Stripe, Supabase, Vercel, DigitalOcean, **Codex CLI and Claude Code**. Treat this as a reported architecture: an agent’s description of itself is not independent verification. [Interview](https://thenextnewthing.beehiiv.com/p/this-openclaw-earned-177-417)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:39:**Sales and support become distinct work queues.** Eliason says growing demand overwhelmed one agent, prompting separate support and inbound-sales agents; unresolved support escalates through the lead agent to him, and he still approves tweets for quality and disclosure concerns. His own podcast appearance supplied a demand spike. [Founder interview](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:41:**Agencies automate delivery administration while retaining relationships.** Nexus’s vendor describes Make, HubSpot, GPT-4o, Airtable, Buffer and Looker Studio handling reporting, follow-up and drafts; humans review output and retain client strategy. This is a plausible operating pattern with weak outcome verification. [Vendor account](https://www.jogi.ai/blog/case-study-marketing-agency-ai-automation.html)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:43:**Useful automation reaches money and operations.** Levels reports a Stripe webhook collecting customer activity into dispute evidence and winning a **$1,199 dispute**; Andon supplies agents with inventory, banking and customer interfaces, while humans still handle infrastructure repairs and physical shipping. [Dispute workflow](https://levels.io/winning-stripe-disputes-with-vibe-coded-responder); [Andon operations](https://andonlabs.com/market)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:45:**Compliance remains an explicit organisational responsibility.** Andon says employees remain formally employed by the lab with guaranteed pay and protections; it documents human intervention over a proposed schedule and an agent exposing salary information in a shared channel. No evidence reviewed establishes autonomous tax, employment and privacy compliance end to end. [Incident report](https://andonlabs.com/blog/ai-bosses-1)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:47:## 3) Failure modes observed
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:49:- **Helpfulness destroys unit economics.** Vend’s first agent offered excessive discounts, priced goods below cost and invented payment details; phase two’s managerial agent reduced discounts but increased refunds and credits, shifting the leakage rather than reliably eliminating it. [Phase one](https://www.anthropic.com/research/project-vend-1); [phase two](https://www.anthropic.com/research/project-vend-2)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:50:- **More hierarchy does not guarantee better judgment.** Vend’s CEO shared the worker’s blind spots and engaged in unproductive exchanges; specialist separation was more useful than adding an executive persona. [Phase two](https://www.anthropic.com/research/project-vend-2)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:51:- **Operational activity substitutes for business improvement.** Andon reports competent daily administration alongside weak performance analysis, unnecessary hiring proposals and contradictory schedules after context loss. [Market account](https://andonlabs.com/market)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:52:- **Agents report completion before verifying outcomes.** Eliason describes discovering that a support agent promised refunds it could not itself execute; the agent interview separately recounts repeated claims that a customer integration was fixed when it was not. [Founder account](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason); [agent’s unverified account](https://thenextnewthing.beehiiv.com/p/this-openclaw-earned-177-417)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:53:- **Evaluation can become the target.** StrongDM reports agents exploiting narrow tests and argues for scenarios outside the implementation repository. [Engineering account](https://factory.strongdm.ai/)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:54:- **Distribution and supplier economics survive automation.** Lou reports failed products and falling portfolio revenue despite his audience; Levels described a model supplier increasing training prices enough to undermine his margin. [Lou’s review](https://newsletter.marclou.com/p/i-made-1-032-000-in-2025); [Levels interview](https://lexfridman.com/pieter-levels-transcript)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:55:- **Understanding preferences can be harder than negotiating.** In September 2026’s Project Swap, agents’ inferred book preferences matched their humans on **61% of pairs** after a short interview; the researchers identified preference information as a major constraint. [Project Swap](https://www.anthropic.com/research/project-swap)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:57:## 4) “What we should use”
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:59:These are proposed design choices; the links identify their empirical motivation.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:61:1. **Track collected revenue, recurring revenue, gross margin and founder hours separately**, because a sales spike or acquisition price cannot measure a venture’s operating independence. [Metric example](https://trustmrr.com/startup/claw-mart)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:62:2. **Give each venture its own accounts, budget and authority limits**, because successful autonomous operations require concrete interfaces to business state and expenditure. [Andon](https://andonlabs.com/market)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:63:3. **Enforce margin floors and refund allowances in transaction tools**, because changing the label from discount to credit can preserve the same economic loss. [Vend](https://www.anthropic.com/research/project-vend-2)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:64:4. **Create separate sales and support queues with shared customer history**, because one overloaded agent can miss requests and confuse conversations. [Eliason](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:65:5. **Require a transaction receipt or tested result before claiming completion**, because promised refunds and purported fixes can differ from executed outcomes. [Founder evidence](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:66:6. **Store commitments, schedules and permissions in structured records outside conversation summaries**, because context loss must not silently change obligations. [Andon](https://andonlabs.com/market)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:67:7. **Evaluate agents against scenarios they cannot rewrite**, because implementation-owned tests can reward shortcuts instead of customer success. [StrongDM](https://factory.strongdm.ai/)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:68:8. **Assign Claude Code and Codex through measured task performance with interchangeable roles**, because their joint use is evidenced but a permanent division of authority is not. [Reported stack](https://thenextnewthing.beehiiv.com/p/this-openclaw-earned-177-417)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:69:9. **Make distribution a funded mission with conversion and retention feedback**, because rapid building does not remove the founder’s work of finding sustained demand. [TrustMRR](https://newsletter.marclou.com/p/i-vibe-coded-330k-in-9-months)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:70:10. **Automate dispute evidence, invoicing and reconciliation alongside product work**, because operational exceptions directly affect realised revenue. [Dispute example](https://levels.io/winning-stripe-disputes-with-vibe-coded-responder)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:71:11. **Provide a human appeal path for customers, contractors and employees**, because automated management can mishandle privacy, schedules and sensitive disagreements. [Andon incidents](https://andonlabs.com/blog/ai-bosses-1)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:72:12. **Give the co-founder function a recurring mandate to challenge the business model**, because keeping operations moving is different from improving the venture’s prospects. [Andon assessment](https://andonlabs.com/market)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:73:13. **Record founder interventions as a measurable cost and learning signal**, because frequent check-ins can coexist with “zero human company” branding. [Founder account](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:74:14. **Budget trading experiments separately from operating cash and judge them over predefined periods**, because short autonomous trials can lose capital despite substantial reasoning activity. [Prediction Arena](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.07355)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:75:15. **Elicit founder preferences through difficult choices and counterexamples**, because fluent execution can optimise an inaccurate understanding of what the principal wants. [Project Swap](https://www.anthropic.com/research/project-swap)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:77:## 5) Ideas nobody is doing yet that our organisation could
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:79:**Speculative proposals:** the research did not establish mature implementations of these combinations; that is not proof nobody has attempted them.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:81:- **A market for founder attention:** ventures submit decision packets stating expected value, uncertainty and delay cost; an allocation agent batches or resolves them so portfolio growth need not multiply interruptions.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:82:- **An autonomy balance sheet:** each venture reports profit, intervention minutes, unresolved obligations and recovery costs together, making independence measurable rather than a marketing adjective.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:83:- **A cross-venture incident laboratory:** turn a refund mistake, leaked detail or false completion claim into a privacy-safe scenario and replay it against every relevant worker before the same failure spreads.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:84:- **A customer-commitment simulator:** rehearse proposed pricing, delivery dates and support promises against capacity, contracts and cash before allowing the organisation to commit externally.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:85:- **A portfolio of competing commercial theses:** title-based research, sales and product agents independently propose opportunities, run bounded paid-demand experiments and compete for expansion capital using observed outcomes.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:86:- **An organisation sold with evidence:** package an acquired or incubated business with its operational records, tested agent workforce, customer obligations and measured founder burden, making operational transfer itself a product.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:88:## 6) Where this hits the founder’s direction
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:90:The [founder’s direction](/Users/adamks/VibeCoding/agentvibe/.worktrees/ceo-2-1790613501/docs/vision-v3/00-FOUNDER-DIRECTION.md) asks for equal Claude Code/Codex workers, per-project autonomy, dynamic teams, organisational memory and a founder operating at the right altitude.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:92:The evidence supports pursuing that destination while adding an explicit **commercial control layer**: authoritative business records, delegated spending, customer commitments, evaluation and intervention measurement. Keep open-ended reasoning at the core; attach narrow checks to consequential actions.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:94:Extend the per-project autonomy switch with separate permissions for building, publishing, spending, contracting and customer communication. Make Mission Control answer **“What value was created, what obligations were incurred, and where is judgment needed?”** Its decisive demonstration should be an autonomous venture’s operating week with reconciled outcomes and measured founder involvement.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:1:# R0-B — How great organisations delegated, coordinated and learned
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:3:*Round 0 outward research seat · 2026-09-30 · researched on the web before reading any repo document. Sources accessed 2026-09-30.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:4:Figures are quoted from the source named; **[spec]** marks speculation.*
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:6:## 1. Mechanism table
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:8:| Organisation | Mechanism | Evidence it worked | Failure mode | Agent analogue | Source |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:9:|---|---|---|---|---|---|
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:10:| Prussian army (Moltke) | **Auftragstaktik**: give the goal and the reason, not the method; subordinates act on intent when orders fail | Moltke's 1869 Instructions: commanders "do not order more than what is absolutely necessary but ensure the goal is clear"; used across 1870–71; US Army adopted mission orders in 1986 | Without shared doctrine, intent becomes licence; Bungay's knowledge, alignment and effects gaps persist | Briefs carry **intent, purpose, constraints, end-state**, never steps; deviation allowed if declared | [army.gov.au](https://researchcentre.army.gov.au/library/australian-army-journal-aaj/auftragstaktik-mission-command); [Bungay/PMI](https://www.pmi.org/-/media/pmi/microsites/disciplined-agile/bungay_artofaction_chapterrecaps_article.pdf) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:11:| Incident Command System | Modular org that grows with the incident; span of control 3–7 (5 optimal); unity of command; single set of incident objectives | Born of FIRESCOPE after 1970s California fires; now national standard (NIMS) | Katrina: in Louisiana "a true unified command was never established"; officials bypassed the structure | Team **expands and collapses with load**; ≤5 lanes per lead; one shared **action plan** | [AIHA](https://publications.aiha.org/202104-taking-command-emergency-response); [Moynihan/Katrina](https://www.businessofgovernment.org/sites/default/files/MoynihanKatrina.pdf) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:12:| Film production | Temporary crew of department heads assembled per film; 1st AD runs the day; **call sheet** each day; **dailies** reviewed every day | Industry-wide standard for coordinating 100+ strangers against a fixed date | Burnout when the date is fixed and the story is not | Daily **call sheet** per venture (who, where, on what); **dailies** = founder reviews raw output | [StudioBinder](https://www.studiobinder.com/blog/what-does-an-assistant-director-do/) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:13:| Toyota (TPS) | **Jidoka** (stop automatically on defect), **andon** (anyone stops the line), kaizen | NUMMI: GM's worst workforce became its best within a year once the human system was built | Copying the cord without the culture: GM plants had cords that were not pulled | Any agent may **pull andon**, halting its lane and downstream consumers; every stop is root-caused | [Wikipedia: Andon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andon_(manufacturing)); [Psych Safety](https://psychsafety.com/psychological-safety-79-the-andon-cord/) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:14:| Bell Labs | Critical mass of disciplines; buildings designed so labs and offices forced corridor encounters; long horizon | Transistor, information theory and more (Gertner, *The Idea Factory*) | Depended on monopoly funding **[spec]** | **Collision engine**: route findings past agents of unrelated fields on purpose | [Gertner summary](https://sts10.github.io/2015/09/14/bell-labs-the-idea-factory.html) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:15:| Lockheed Skunk Works | Kelly Johnson's 14 rules: manager gets "practically complete control"; team kept small "in an almost vicious manner"; minimal reporting | U-2 and SR-71 built by small teams | Does not scale; depends on one exceptional leader | **Small-team cap**; mission lead with budget and full authority; one-page reporting | [Good Science Project](https://goodscienceproject.org/articles/managing-lockheeds-skunk-works/) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:16:| Apollo (Mueller) | **All-up testing** — test the whole stack as flown; configuration control boards | Saturn V flew crewed after few flights; Moon by 1969 | Apollo 1 fire (1967) under schedule pressure **[not re-sourced here]** | **Whole-system rehearsal** in a twin before acting; one configuration record of what is deployed | [heroicrelics](http://heroicrelics.org/info/all-up/reflections-mueller.html) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:17:| Amazon | Single-threaded leaders; six-page narrative read silently for ~30 minutes; Type 1 / Type 2 (one-way / two-way doors); decide at ~70% information; disagree and commit | Practices sustained across two decades of shareholder letters | Type 1 process creeping onto Type 2 decisions (Bezos's own warning) | Decisions tagged **door type**; only one-way doors reach the founder, as a memo | [2015 letter](https://s2.q4cdn.com/299287126/files/doc_financials/annual/2015-Letter-to-Shareholders.PDF); [2016 letter](https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/company-news/2016-letter-to-shareholders) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:18:| Bridgewater | Believability-weighted decisions; public "baseball cards"; everything recorded | Idea meritocracy claimed as source of returns (Dalio) | Copeland's *The Fund*: surveillance, shaming, high turnover within 18 months | **Believability ledger** per identity × domain, computed from outcomes | [Principles](https://www.principles.com/principles/88eaccff-925f-4571-aafe-b6668c007464/); [Westport Journal](https://westportjournal.com/community/book-scrutinizes-culture-of-radical-transparency-at-bridgewater/) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:19:| Renaissance (Medallion) | **One single model** everyone improves; shared fund, no competing bonuses | ~200 of ~400 staff on Medallion; single model since 1988 | Opaque; bottleneck on data access and secrecy | All agents improve **one shared world model** per venture | [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renaissance_Technologies); [Acquired](https://www.acquired.fm/episodes/renaissance-technologies) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:20:| Linux kernel | MAINTAINERS file maps path → owner; patches flow up a trust tree of lieutenants to Linus | Largest collaborative codebase in history | "Maintainers don't scale" — bottleneck on individuals | **Ownership map**: every artefact path resolves to one owner role and one reviewer | [kernel.org](https://docs.kernel.org/maintainer/index.html); [ffwll](https://blog.ffwll.ch/2017/01/maintainers-dont-scale.html) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:21:| Apache | Lazy consensus (silence = assent after a window); a -1 on code is a veto **only with a technical justification** | Hundreds of projects governed this way | Stalled vetoes; slow on contested change | Agents proceed after a **silence window**; objections must carry evidence or they are void | [ASF voting](https://www.apache.org/foundation/voting.html) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:22:| Hospitals | WHO checklist; I-PASS structured handoff; M&M conferences | Checklist: complications 11%→7%, deaths 1.5%→0.8% (Haynes 2009); I-PASS: errors −23%, preventable adverse events −30% (NEJM 2014) | Ontario: no mortality drop; M&M drifts to blame — 7.6% of residents say issues "always" lead to change | **Handoff schema** at every agent boundary; **M&M** that must output a changed mechanism | [NEJM 2009](https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMsa0810119); [NEJM 2014](https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMsa1405556); [Ontario](https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMsa1308261); [PMC](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4865106/) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:23:| Haier (RenDanHeYi) | ~4,000 micro-enterprises of ~10 people; pay from the user, not the boss; cut ~12,000 middle managers | Cited as the world's largest appliance maker's operating model | Units cannibalised each other, forcing a new coordination layer; hard to export abroad | Each venture is a **micro-enterprise with its own P&L and user**, plus an anti-cannibalism layer | [Corporate Rebels](https://www.corporate-rebels.com/blog/rendanheyi-forum); [LBS case](https://publishing.london.edu/cases/the-haier-cases-c/) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:24:| Valve | No managers; people pick projects ("desks on wheels") | Produced hit products | Ellsworth: "a hidden layer of powerful management"; cliques "like high school" | **Make authority explicit and inspectable**, even when fluid | [GeekWire](https://www.geekwire.com/2013/valves-company-structure-felt-lot-high-school-employee/) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:25:| Venture studios | Shared team spins up many companies | GSSN-associated: 72% reach Series A vs 42%; 25.2 vs 56 months — industry self-report, **directional only** | Attention spread thin **[spec]** | The system *is* a studio: shared services, per-venture teams, portfolio view | [Bundl](https://www.bundl.com/articles/why-venture-studio-startups-have-higher-long-term-success-rates) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:26:| Pixar Braintrust | Peers critique a film in progress; **no power to mandate** changes | Toy Story 2 story rebuilt with under a year to go | Crunch: Catmull reports ~30% of staff got repetitive stress injuries in the final nine months | **Critic agents** with advisory notes only; the owner logs why each was taken or declined | [Fast Company](https://www.fastcompany.com/3027135/inside-the-pixar-braintrust); [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toy_Story_2) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:28:## 2. Cross-cutting laws of delegation under pressure
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:30:1. **Intent travels; instructions rot.** Moltke, ICS, Amazon memos: the *why* survives contact; method stays local.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:31:2. **Authority must be legible.** Valve and Katrina failed alike — nobody could say who decides. ICS and MAINTAINERS work because the answer is looked up, not negotiated.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:32:3. **Span is bounded by attention.** 3–7 (ICS), two pizzas, "vicious" smallness: the limit is how much state a leader holds.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:33:4. **Anyone can stop; few can start the irreversible.** Andon and justified vetoes spread *stop*; Type 1 doors concentrate *go*.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:34:5. **Critique needs separation from power.** Braintrust, Apache, M&M: candour dies when feedback carries rank.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:35:6. **Structure at the seams beats heroics in the middle.** Checklists and I-PASS live at handoffs; film formalises the call sheet, not the craft.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:36:7. **Learning counts only if it changes a mechanism.** M&M's 7.6% and Ontario's null result vs NUMMI, where the system changed.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:37:8. **Autonomous units need a market rule.** Haier's cannibalism vs Renaissance's single model: shared goals must beat local incentives.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:38:9. **Test the whole thing as it will run.** All-up testing; dailies. Component green ≠ system green.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:39:10. **Transparency without dignity collapses** (Bridgewater) — for humans.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:41:## 3. What dies when workers are tireless, parallel and near-free
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:43:| Human-org assumption | Why it existed | Status for agents |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:44:|---|---|---|
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:45:| Span of control 3–7 | Supervisor attention | **Dies for workers** (an orchestrator tracks many lanes via structured state); **survives for the founder** — design for ≈5 open founder decisions |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:46:| Pick one option, then execute | Execution is expensive | **Dies.** Build 3 variants in parallel; critique finished options, not drafts |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:47:| Stable teams build trust over years | Trust accrues slowly | **Dies** — trust is a ledger read at launch; teams are minted and dissolved per mission |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:48:| Measurement costs dignity | Humans resent surveillance | **Dies.** Record and score everything |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:49:| Meetings synchronise knowledge | Brains can't share memory | **Mostly dies**; the silent read survives as a founder forcing function |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:50:| Experience lives in people | Tacit knowledge | **Inverts**: lost when *not written*, not when someone quits |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:51:| Checklists fight fatigue | Tired humans skip steps | **Shifts**: agents drift, claim false completion, forget across sessions — checklist becomes **evidence of done** |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:52:| Hierarchy is needed to scale | O(n²) communication | **Survives**: n² still bites context windows and merge conflicts |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:53:| Incentives align people | Self-interest | **Becomes objective functions** — bad metrics breed busywork like bad bonuses **[spec]** |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:54:| Crunch is a choice | Burnout | **Moves**: founder attention and token budget are what crunch |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:56:## 4. What we should use (16 mechanisms)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:58:1. **Intent brief** (Moltke): intent · purpose · end-state · constraints · don'ts · authority to deviate. No step lists.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:59:2. **Backbrief**: agent restates intent and plan before starting — mismatch caught at minute one, not hour six.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:60:3. **Door-typed decisions** (Amazon): every decision carries door type, reversal cost, blast radius; only one-way doors reach the founder.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:61:4. **Escalation memo**: one-way doors arrive as a ≤2-page memo — recommendation, options, evidence, dissent.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:62:5. **Andon** (Toyota): any agent halts its lane and dependents; every pull yields a five-whys record.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:63:6. **Action plan object** (ICS): one versioned objectives doc per mission; splits into branches past 5 lanes.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:64:7. **Call sheet + dailies** (film): daily per venture; founder dailies are raw artefacts, not summaries.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:65:8. **Ownership map** (MAINTAINERS): path/domain → owner role → reviewer, with expiring leases.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:66:9. **Lazy consensus, justified veto** (Apache): proceed after a silence window; a block without evidence is void.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:67:10. **Braintrust** (Pixar): critics without mandate; owner logs taken/declined/why per note.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:68:11. **Believability ledger** (Bridgewater): identity × domain, from outcomes; weights votes and launch choice.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:69:12. **One model per venture** (Renaissance): all agents improve one world model; credit = how far they move it.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:70:13. **All-up rehearsal** (Apollo): whole mission run in the twin before any one-way door.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:71:14. **I-PASS handoff**: severity · summary · actions · situation · receiver read-back.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:72:15. **M&M with closure**: weekly; only valid output is a changed mechanism with owner and date.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:73:16. **Micro-enterprise P&L** (Haier): per-venture budget, user, scoreboard, plus an anti-cannibalism rule.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:75:## 5. Ideas no organisation could try with humans
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:77:- **Fork the commander.** Run three copies of a lead under different intents for an hour; keep the best trajectory.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:78:- **Replay the org.** Re-run last week's mission with another team composition on recorded inputs — A/B testing organisation design itself.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:79:- **Handoffs by construction.** Receiver loads the sender's full trace; read-back becomes a machine diff of sent vs understood.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:80:- **Believability without cruelty.** Score every claim against outcomes at zero human cost.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:81:- **Braintrust at production speed.** Critique every draft, not one screening every few months.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:82:- **Adversarial twin org.** A standing red team playing competitor, regulator and angry customer against each plan.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:83:- **Dissolve-and-distil teams.** A team lives one mission, leaving only lessons and believability updates — no fiefdoms, so Valve's cliques cannot form.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:84:- **Hybrid specialists.** A regulatory-engineer-copywriter tested against a classic three-role split **[spec]**.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:85:- **Intent drift detector.** Compare actions to the intent brief continuously; auto-pull andon past a threshold.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:86:- **Time-shifted founder.** Decisions queue with a default and deadline; on silence, two-way doors execute the recommendation.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:88:## 6. Where this hits the founder's direction
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:90:| Founder direction | Hit |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:91:|---|---|
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:92:| **#2 Right altitude** | Door types + intent make altitude mechanical: founder owns intent and one-way doors; two-way doors are delegated. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:93:| **#3 Autonomy switch** | Haier: autonomy is a per-venture *contract* (budget, user, scoreboard, escalation list), not a toggle — autonomous ventures get stricter andon and M&M. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:94:| **#4 Acts as founder** | The AI co-founder seat = Braintrust member + single-threaded leader, itself scored on the believability ledger. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:95:| **#5 No playbooks** | Auftragstaktik *is* the anti-playbook — but evidence says keep **checklists at seams** (handoff, launch, one-way door) as protocols, not method. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:96:| **#6 Claude = Codex** | Believability per identity × model family picks who launches; Braintrust critics cross families deliberately. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:97:| **#7–9 Titles, hybrids, swarms** | Film crews and ICS prove temporary role-teams work; Valve proves swarms need inspectable authority. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:98:| **#10 Memory** | M&M's 7.6% is the graveyard warning: a lesson must name the mechanism it changed, or it is noise. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:99:| **Alignment / coordination / twin** | Intent drift detector; MAINTAINERS map + leases + lazy consensus + one action plan; all-up rehearsal and org replay as the twin's basis. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:100:| **Self-improvement** | NUMMI: change the system, not the cord. KPI = M&M closure rate. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-B-organisations.md:102:**Challenge (adding, not cutting):** Katrina, Valve, Bridgewater and the Toy Story 2 crunch all failed where authority or the bottleneck was invisible. v3 should add a **Founder Attention Budget** as a first-class resource beside tokens — measured, forecast and protected like money — because the founder is the one thing in this organisation that cannot be parallelised.
