docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:61:## 3. Memory systems
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:63:| System | Model | Forgetting / consolidation | Benchmark reality |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:64:|---|---|---|---|
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:65:| **Anthropic memory stores** (Managed Agents, beta) | Path-addressed files mounted at /mnt/memory; ≤8 stores per session, ≤100 kB per memory, ≤10k memories per store | **Immutable version per write** (30-day history), redact, sha256 preconditions, read_only mounts. **Dreaming** writes a *new* consolidated store instead of mutating the old one ([docs](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/memory)) | None public. The docs warn that injected content persists as "trusted memory" |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:66:| Anthropic memory tool | Client-side file directory | none | — |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:67:| **Letta** | Shared, size-capped memory blocks; Letta Code rewrites its own system prompt | **Sleep-time agents** consolidate while idle ([docs](https://docs.letta.com/guides/agents/architectures/sleeptime/)); the paper reports about 5× less test-time compute at equal accuracy ([2504.13171](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.13171)) | LoCoMo about 74–83 (third party) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:68:| **Zep / Graphiti** | Temporal KG, **bi-temporal edges** (valid/invalid + learned times) | Invalidates rather than deletes, so it can answer "what was true when" | Claims 94.7% LoCoMo; a third party measured 75.1%. LongMemEval R@5 63.8% |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:69:| **Mem0** | LLM extract → ADD/UPDATE/DELETE over vectors (+ graph) | LLM-decided; no temporal validity | Self-reported about 93–94% LongMemEval; **independent OSS test: 32.4%** ([dev.to](https://dev.to/everest_an/-i-benchmarked-ai-agent-memory-in-2026-and-the-numbers-tell-a-different-story-than-the-marketing-2ae4), by an author who maintains a competitor) |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:70:| **Cognee** | Graph + vector + relational; 14 retrieval modes | "memify" prunes stale nodes and reweights edges by usage | Vendor claims only |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:71:| **LangMem** | Semantic + **procedural** | Rewrites prompts from trajectories | — |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:73:**Evidence on forgetting (2026):**
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:74:- **ForgetEval** ([2606.15903](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.15903)): 13 configurations, 385 adversarial cases. Deterministic
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:75:  stores score 0–5% on canonicalization. An LLM at write time fixes that (100%) but scores **0% on intent-aware deletion**.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:76:  An LLM *at mutation time* scores 78–85% on deletion and **91.7–93.2% overall**, at $0.17 per run. Where the model sits
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:77:  decides which forgetting failures you can recover from.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:78:- **SleepGate** ([2603.14517](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.14517)): conflict-gated forgetting keeps 97–99.5% retrieval under
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:79:  interference, where every baseline stays below 18%. Superseded facts actively damage retrieval.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:80:- Forgetting "should be governed, not incidental" ([SSGM 2603.11768](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.11768)). New benchmarks
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:81:  (MemoryArena, AMA-Bench, EvoMemBench, FiFA) score use and privacy-aware forgetting, not just recall.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:82:- **Nobody measures whether a memory was read and whether reading it changed an outcome.**
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-C-tooling-ecosystem.md:84:## 4. Voice / phone stack for reaching the founder
